WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:03.567
Here is one defensible e-commerce analysis direction.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:08.337
Device type is nominal and works naturally with one-hot encoding.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:13.092
Membership tier is ordinal when the business defines a real ranking.

00:00:13.092 --> 00:00:15.922
Session duration is a ratio measurement.

00:00:15.922 --> 00:00:18.992
Purchase count is a discrete ratio count.

00:00:18.992 --> 00:00:24.987
Weekday often behaves as a cyclical category because Sunday connects back to Monday.

00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:30.882
Revenue should use an exact numeric storage type, with currency documented separately.

00:00:30.882 --> 00:00:38.272
Connect this idea to a university analyzing student records, surveys, and learning-platform activity.

00:00:38.272 --> 00:00:44.042
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:51.782
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:57.467
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:03.376
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
